{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recording-tree-020-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/TreeCommitTests.cs","line":920,"method":"CommitTree_AlreadyConcludedOrbitingChild_StaysImmutable","category":"T1","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RecordingStore.cs:1258; remove the isFirstCommit guard -> still green because the second CommitTree returns at the reference-equal duplicate skip (RecordingStore.cs:1000-1015) before ApplyRewindProvisionalMergeStates runs; forcing the pass to re-run AND dropping the guard -> red","what_it_asserts":"After manually sealing child2 Immutable, a second CommitTree(tree) leaves child2 Immutable and the slot tip closed.","why_weak":"The re-commit never reaches the promotion pass the comment claims to exercise, so the first-commit-guard claim is unwitnessed; that guard is covered via the seam in CollapseSealMergeStateRegressionTests.cs:150/191.","proposed_action":"Replace the second CommitTree(tree) with RecordingStore.ApplyRewindProvisionalMergeStatesForTesting(tree) and assert child2 stays Immutable, or delete the cell.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
